 "_doc": "Medusa, boss (GAME_DESIGN.md: The Aegean Shore bosses; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_boss_medusa.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. From Pseudo-Apollodorus, Bibliotheca 2.4.2: the Gorgons had heads twined about with the scales of serpents, great tusks like swine's, and hands of bronze (their wings of gold are left out at the owner's request, 10/31/2026, as in Ovid's telling); and Ovid, Metamorphoses 4 (snakes for hair). In the ancient sources and art she has a woman's legs; she has a serpent's tail instead at the owner's request (10/31/2026), the well-known modern image. The short chiton is how archaic Greek vase paintings and temple reliefs show her. Bigger than a Hero (a boss).",
